{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-07-11T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In France, Port de Saint-Goustan lies just below Auray’s upper town, where a narrow inlet meets the estuary leading into the Gulf of Morbihan. The harbour sits along the Auray River In the 13th century, the Dukes of Brittany built a bridge, a port and a castle here; the fortress has vanished, but cobbled quays and timber-framed houses still line the waterfront.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AurayBrittany_EN-GB4284557242_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AurayBrittany_EN-GB4284557242_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Just across the channel: Port de Saint-Goustan","Title":"Port de Saint-Goustan, Auray, Brittany, France","Copyright":"© Rolf E. Staerk/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/47.664311,-2.977482/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=47.664311,-2.977482;S9;Port de Saint-Goustan, Auray, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260711_AurayBrittany\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Auray+Saint-Goustan+France&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260710_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260711_AurayBrittany"},"Ssd":"20260711","Name":"AurayBrittany","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"4284557242","FullDateString":"11 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some monasteries begin with a grand plan. Llanthony Priory, however, owes its origin to a knight who lost his way. Nestled in the Vale of Ewyas beneath the Black Mountains, the priory is a 900-year-old Augustinian ruin. History has it that a Norman knight, William de Lacy, stumbled upon a ruined chapel dedicated to St David while hunting. Captivated by the solitude, he abandoned his military life to become a hermit, leading to the foundation of the monastery around 1100.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LlanthonyPriory2026_EN-GB5365093988_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LlanthonyPriory2026_EN-GB5365093988_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A valley of ruins and legends","Title":"Llanthony Priory, Black Mountains area, Monmouthshire, Wales","Copyright":"© Chris Griffiths/Moment/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.94473,-3.036616/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.94473,-3.036616;S9;Llanthony Priory, Monmouthshire, Wales&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260710_LlanthonyPriory2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Llanthony+Priory&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260709_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260710_LlanthonyPriory2026"},"Ssd":"20260710","Name":"LlanthonyPriory2026","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"5365093988","FullDateString":"10 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Sunlight cuts through drifting clouds and settles on the terraced slopes of Sapa, where rice fields cascade down the mountainsides like a living staircase. Located in Vietnam's Lào Cai province, this highland region is shaped as much by human hands as by nature. Generations of farmers from local ethnic communities such as the Hmong have carved and maintained these terraces for centuries, guiding water across steep hillsides to sustain each growing season.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SapaVietnam_EN-GB1434771886_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SapaVietnam_EN-GB1434771886_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Tradition in every step","Title":"Rice fields at Sapa, Lào Cai, Vietnam","Copyright":"© Anujak Jaimook/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/22.374456,103.842076/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=22.374456,103.842076;S9;Sapa, Lào Cai, Vietnam&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260709_SapaVietnam\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lao+Cai+Vietnam&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260708_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260709_SapaVietnam"},"Ssd":"20260709","Name":"SapaVietnam","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1434771886","FullDateString":"9 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Set in Guatemala's western highlands, Lake Atitlán fills a vast volcanic caldera. Its deep blue waters are framed by steep crater walls and the cone-shaped volcanoes Atitlán, Tolimán and San Pedro. Wooden piers stretch into the still lake, emphasising the contrast between its calm surface and the rugged terrain shaped by volcanic activity.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeAtitlan_EN-GB6255247922_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeAtitlan_EN-GB6255247922_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Echoes of a volcanic past","Title":"Lake Atitlán, Guatemala","Copyright":"© shayes17/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/14.702858,-91.194628/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=14.702858,-91.194628;S9;Lake Atitlán, Sololá, Guatemala&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260708_LakeAtitlan\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+Atitlan+Guatemala&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260707_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260708_LakeAtitlan"},"Ssd":"20260708","Name":"LakeAtitlan","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6255247922","FullDateString":"8 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A bill like a multitool and plumage full of colour—the plate-billed mountain toucan is one of the Andes' most distinctive birds. It lives in the humid mountain forests of Ecuador and southwestern Colombia, perfectly adapted to life high in the canopy.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MountainToucanOrchids_EN-GB2911291133_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MountainToucanOrchids_EN-GB2911291133_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Colour, craft and canopy life","Title":"Plate-billed mountain toucan with orchids, Ecuador","Copyright":"© Murray Cooper/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The plate-billed mountain toucan's colourful bill features a pale yellow 'plate,' a rare trait that gives this species its name.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260707_MountainToucanOrchids\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Plate-billed+mountain+toucan&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260706_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260707_MountainToucanOrchids"},"Ssd":"20260707","Name":"MountainToucanOrchids","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"2911291133","FullDateString":"7 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Founded by Greek settlers from Corinth around 734 BCE, the Italian city of Syracuse, on the island of Sicily, grew into one of the ancient Mediterranean's great powers and is now part of a UNESCO World Heritage Site, 'Syracuse and the Rocky Necropolis of Pantalica.' It is forever linked to Archimedes, whose genius still shapes its identity, and to Plato, who came to Syracuse hoping philosophy might shape political life. That layered past still feels tangible at Castello Maniace, a seafront fortress built for Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II in the 13th century, which can still be admired today.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SyracuseItaly_EN-GB9688094986_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SyracuseItaly_EN-GB9688094986_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A city written in centuries","Title":"Syracuse, Sicily, Italy","Copyright":"© Balate Dorin/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.067122,15.285311/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.067122,15.285311;S9;Syracuse, Sicily, Italy&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260706_SyracuseItaly\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Syracuse+Sicily&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260705_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260706_SyracuseItaly"},"Ssd":"20260706","Name":"SyracuseItaly","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"9688094986","FullDateString":"6 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In southeastern France, on the Valensole Plateau, summer arrives in waves of purple and blue. Valensole—one of the largest plateaus in the region—lies in the Verdon Regional Natural Park between the Durance and Asse valleys, near the Gorges du Verdon and its lakes. From mid-June to early July, depending on altitude and weather, lavender and lavandin bloom and transform the landscape into one of Provence's most recognisable sights. The air carries a sharp, dry and unmistakably Mediterranean scent.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LavenderRows_EN-GB8618053489_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LavenderRows_EN-GB8618053489_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Sea of purple","Title":"Lavender rows, Plateau de Valensole, Provence, France","Copyright":"© Robert Harding/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/43.857636,5.974437/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=43.857636,5.974437;S9;Plateau de Valensole, Provence, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260705_LavenderRows\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lavandula&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260704_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260705_LavenderRows"},"Ssd":"20260705","Name":"LavenderRows","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"8618053489","FullDateString":"5 Jul 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Reflected in still water, the Rakotzbrücke—commonly known as the Devil's Bridge—forms a near-perfect stone circle in Saxony, Germany. Commissioned in 1860, the narrow basalt structure was carefully engineered so that its arch and reflection align to form a seamless ring when the lake is still. Made from locally sourced volcanic stone, it reflects precise design rather than practical function, its striking geometry intended purely for visual effect. A popular photo subject, it has also appeared in films, including 'The Matrix Resurrections' (2021). Today, the fragile bridge can only be admired from the shore, as crossing is prohibited to preserve it.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DevilsBridge_EN-GB3657419694_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DevilsBridge_EN-GB3657419694_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Going full circle","Title":"Devil's Bridge in Rhododendron Park Kromlau, Saxony, Germany","Copyright":"© Mike Mareen/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.53661,14.640453/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.53661,14.640453;S9;Devil's Bridge, Kromlau, Saxony, Germany&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260718_DevilsBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Devils+Bridge+Kromlau&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260717_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260718_DevilsBridge"},"Ssd":"20260718","Name":"DevilsBridge","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"3657419694","FullDateString":"18 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"On the remote northeastern tip of Crete, Greece, lies a quiet corner far from typical tourist routes. Today's image shows Vai Beach, a broad curve of golden sand bordered by calm, shallow waters of the Aegean Sea. With sunbeds, umbrellas and showers, it's ideal for swimming, relaxing or enjoying the peaceful atmosphere. But what truly sets Vai apart is just beyond the sand: Europe's largest natural palm grove. It consists of more than 5,000 Cretan date palm trees, a species native to Crete and parts of Turkey.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VaiUmbrellas_EN-GB3361752741_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VaiUmbrellas_EN-GB3361752741_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A Greek escape","Title":"Blue sunbeds on a sandy beach in Vai, Crete, Greece","Copyright":"© borchee/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/35.30972,24.89333/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=35.30972,24.89333;S9;Crete, Greece&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":"/maps?ty=30&q=crete%20greece&satid=id.sid%3Aa898a116-f402-c866-449a-1e49d7c0585b&vdpid=7247538364818128897&mb=36.013862~23.514471~34.598793~26.318979&cardbg=%23F98745&dt=1749198600000&tt=Crete%2C%20Crete%2C%20Greece&tsts0=%2526ty%253D30%2526q%253Dcrete%252520greece%2526satid%253Did.sid%25253Aa898a116-f402-c866-449a-1e49d7c0585b%2526vdpid%253D7247538364818128897%2526mb%253D36.013862~23.514471~34.598793~26.318979%2526cardbg%253D%252523F98745%2526dt%253D1749198600000&tstt0=Crete%2C%20Crete%2C%20Greece&cp=34.85975~13.56328&lvl=4.98&pi=0&ftst=0&ftics=False&v=2&sV=2&form=hpbal1"},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260717_VaiUmbrellas\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Crete+Greece&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260716_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260717_VaiUmbrellas"},"Ssd":"20260717","Name":"VaiUmbrellas","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"3361752741","FullDateString":"17 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Victoria, a southeastern state of Australia, extends along more than 1,100 miles of mainland coastline shaped by the Southern Ocean. From above, its beaches appear as sweeping bands of pale sand edged by turquoise waters and rugged cliffs. This dynamic interaction of land and sea defines much of the region's appeal. The famous Great Ocean Road traces roughly 150 miles of this shoreline, winding past popular surf spots, forested headlands and seaside towns.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VictoriaBeach_EN-GB5330505184_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VictoriaBeach_EN-GB5330505184_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The land of moving shorelines","Title":"Aerial view of land and ocean, Victoria, Australia","Copyright":"© Nearmap/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-36.850086,144.304291/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-36.850086,144.304291;S9;Victoria, Australia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260716_VictoriaBeach\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Victoria+Australia&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260715_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260716_VictoriaBeach"},"Ssd":"20260716","Name":"VictoriaBeach","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"5330505184","FullDateString":"16 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"If mountains could keep a record of the past, the John Muir Wilderness near Bishop, California, United States, would have plenty to share. Its valleys, lakes and granite formations reveal a history shaped over millions of years. Established in 1964, this vast protected area spans more than 650,000 acres (263,000 hectares) of the Sierra Nevada and is named after naturalist John Muir. Today, parts of the Pacific Crest Trail and John Muir Trail pass through the area, drawing hikers into one of the largest high-elevation wilderness regions in the contiguous United States.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MarieLake_EN-GB7432567016_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MarieLake_EN-GB7432567016_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The reward after the climb","Title":"Marie Lake, John Muir Wilderness near Bishop, California, United States","Copyright":"© Steve Dunleavy/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/36.97615,-118.812278/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=36.97615,-118.812278;S9;John Muir Wilderness, California, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260715_MarieLake\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=John+Muir+Wilderness&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260714_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260715_MarieLake"},"Ssd":"20260715","Name":"MarieLake","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"7432567016","FullDateString":"15 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"On 14 July, Shark Awareness Day asks us to trade movie panic for ocean truth. Sharks have patrolled the seas for more than 420 million years, and as apex predators, they help keep marine ecosystems in balance.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LemonShark_EN-GB6406610577_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LemonShark_EN-GB6406610577_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Fin-tastic truths","Title":"Lemon shark pup in mangrove forest, Eleuthera, Bahamas","Copyright":"© Shane Gross/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The Greenland shark can live up to 400 years, one of the longest lifespans of any vertebrate.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260714_LemonShark\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Shark+Awareness+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260713_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260714_LemonShark"},"Ssd":"20260714","Name":"LemonShark","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6406610577","FullDateString":"14 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"International Rock Day, observed on 13 July, celebrates the geological building blocks beneath our feet and encourages curiosity about how rocks shape Earth's landscapes and history. From the dramatic cliffs of Britain's coastline to vast desert canyons abroad, rocks reveal stories of ancient seas, shifting continents and life over millions of years.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NavajoSandstone_EN-GB4980697300_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NavajoSandstone_EN-GB4980697300_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Born to rock","Title":"Antelope Canyon on the Navajo Nation, east of Page, Arizona, United States","Copyright":"© Mark Skalny/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/40.837774,-118.280526/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=40.837774,-118.280526;S9;Antelope Canyon, Arizona, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260713_NavajoSandstone\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=International+Rock+Day+geology&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260712_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260713_NavajoSandstone"},"Ssd":"20260713","Name":"NavajoSandstone","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"4980697300","FullDateString":"13 Jul 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"If you're looking for Maine in the United States at its wildest, Katahdin Woods and Waters National Monument is hard to beat. Covering around 35,400 hectares of the North Woods, it is a landscape of quiet ponds, winding rivers and dense forests where nature still dominates.",